  "id": "persistent-complex-bereavement-disorder",
  "term": "persistent complex bereavement disorder",
  "definition": "Persistent complex bereavement disorder is a severe, disabling grief reaction that continues without easing for at least 12 months after the death of a significant other. It centers on ongoing yearning or missing the person who died and being preoccupied with the circumstances of the death.",
